# plurx UI structural golden — the portable tier of scripts/ui-baseline.
#
#   regenerate   scripts/ui-baseline --self-host --update
#   verify       make ui-check
#
# COMMITTED ON PURPOSE, and pixel-free on purpose. A PNG hash depends on the
# Chromium build, the rasteriser and the path the fixture library sits at, so a
# committed pixel manifest is red on every machine but the one that wrote it.
# Everything below is a fact about the DOM the app builds, and is therefore the
# same on a Mac, in the sandbox and on a CI runner. Pixel hashes stay in
# target/ui-baseline/pixels.txt and are compared with --baseline, never here.
#
# Format, one fact per line:
#
#   <layout>|<route>@<w>x<h>|<kind>|<key>|<value>
#
#   layout   dark|light etc. are NOT dimensions here — one theme, every layout.
#            `*` marks a fact about the registry rather than about a capture.
#   kind     layout   a registered layout and the surfaces it declares
#            surface  which surfaceClass() a viewport resolves to
#            dom      a structural signature `parent > self`, and how many of
#                     them the route rendered. Tags, ids, sorted classes, role,
#                     tabindex, ARIA state and a bare `text` flag — never text
#                     content, inline style, href, src or value.
#            focus    the Nth tab stop, zero-padded so the order sorts
#            req      an API call the route made, method + path, and how often
#
# Regeneration must be a deliberate act with a diff, never a side effect of a
# normal run — that is why `--update` exists and why a plain run writes only
# into target/. If this file changed and you did not mean it to, the app
# changed.
*|*|layout|catalog|desktop mobile tv
*|*|layout|classic|desktop mobile tv
*|*|layout|theater|desktop mobile tv
*|*|surface|1280x860|desktop
*|*|surface|390x780|mobile
